      "title": "[Kagi Small Web] BOOM",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=kagi.com&amp;sz=128\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=kagi.com&amp;sz=128\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=kagi.com&amp;sz=128\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=kagi.com&amp;sz=128\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<p>There was a brief thunderstorm Thursday evening (enough that the power flickered, and I ran some water to use if it went out completely) and two more yesterday. Now. Guess. I&rsquo;m hearing distant thunder. </p><p>Not <i>unhappy</i> about that, because our Augusts are typically dry as a bone. I will have to run to the field to let the goats off their tethers, though. And, of course, I will wait until it&rsquo;s actually raining, and get myself soaked. yay!</p><p>A popsicle would fix me. I should have a popsicle.</p>",
